  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, there is no evidence to exploit, so the priority is establishing a reliable performance baseline to anchor all future comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the search space: it uses a linear PCA reduction with no learned encoder, no multi-profile aggregation, and no fusion. Running this first gives us (1) a floor performance estimate for the RNA signal under minimal modeling assumptions, (2) a fast and cheap experiment (PCA requires no training), and (3) a clean reference point against which every subsequent change—learned RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), multi-profile aggregation, image modality, and fusion strategies—can be measured. This maximizes the information gained per experiment by isolating the raw data signal before introducing any additional complexity."
